{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_lih5ubhldb5aiy4a7zedjqifbucxpblldnu35sp4ogi35qbr5rsa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All verification complete. Final summary:\n\n## Result: the Rust translation is correct — `src/lib.rs` needed **zero** changes\n\nThe library is small (one 60-line C file, one exported symbol `tritanopia`), which let me verify it **exhaustively** rather than by sampling.\n\n### Phase A — artifacts (all mechanically derived)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` diff **empty both ways**; only `tritanopia` is exported (the other 5 C functions are `static`). Both `.so`s import the *same* `pow@GLIBC_2.29`, so `f64::powf` ≡ C `pow` bit-for-bit. 0 undefined non-libc symbols. No C source was left untranslated; no stubs. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | The C has **no error returns at all** (grep for `RETURN_ERROR`/`return -1`/`NULL`/`assert`/`errno` → zero hits). Its real rejection surface is the 3 implementation-defined `(unsigned char)` casts + 6 strict-`>` thresholds → **15 rows**. E10–E12 (null ptr / enum / length) are N/A *by signature*, justified rather than guessed. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **No** runtime options, no `#ifdef`, no `[features]` → one configuration. 7 branch axes → **28 rows**. |\n\n### Phases B–D — results\n- **Row 26: all 16,777,216 inputs byte-identical, 0 divergences** — the entire input domain, not a sample.\n- 28/28 `CONFIGS.md` rows and 15/15 `ERRORS.md` rows pass, across **8 configurations** (2 feature spellings × debug/release × C `-O0`/`-O2`; the `-O2` object is genuinely different code, `.text` 2159 vs 3077 bytes).\n- The tricky part the translation already got right: C's `(unsigned char)` cast of out-of-range floats is UB, and **11% of all inputs depend on it** — `(0,0,255)→R=93` (from −419.2) and `(255,255,0)→R=13` (from 269.3). Rust's `as u8` would saturate to 0/255; `f32_to_uchar` correctly replicates `cvttss2si`.\n\n### Two real problems I found and fixed (both in the harness, not the translation)\n1. **The suite was passing vacuously.** With `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`, `cargo test` never rebuilds/uplifts the `.so`, so my first three injected bugs \"survived\" against a *stale* library. Fixed with `crate-type = [\"cdylib\",\"rlib\"]`, a mandatory `cargo build` before `cargo test`, and a hard staleness assert in the harness.\n2. **My `run_all.sh` initially reported \"ALL PASSED\" spuriously** because `/tmp` is read-only here, so `tee`/`comm` failed silently. Rewritten to use `$TMPDIR` and **fail closed** (missing log or <41 passing tests ⇒ failure). Verified it goes red in all 8 configs when a bug is injected.\n\nI also corrected one of my own tests: `err_e9` initially asserted \"R must never be 0\", which was wrong — slightly-negative values legitimately truncate to 0. The C was never in question; my test's premise was.\n\n### Anti-vacuity evidence (`./mutation_test.sh`, 15/15 as predicted)\n10 realistic mistranslations are **caught** (saturating cast → 18 failures; `round` vs `trunc` → 28; `12.92→12.29` → 27; f32-vs-f64 gamma math; re-grouping `(R+aG)-bB` → caught *only* by the exhaustive row). 5 **correctly survive**, and I proved each is genuinely equivalent rather than a blind spot — notably the C writes `0.12739886310880f` and `0.12739886341072f`, which **round to the identical f32 bit pattern** `d974023e` (differ by 3e-10 vs f32 spacing 1.5e-8). A source-level literal audit confirms every C constant, both tiny cross-term signs, and the left-to-right grouping match exactly.\n\n`c_src/` is untouched (md5s unchanged; I removed a stray empty `tests/` dir I accidentally created there when my shell cwd drifted)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":780,"cache_read_input_tokens":152472,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":780,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7e1660b-d76b-470b-a9f8-e1b1ddb6ffaf","uuid":"bd7c2a2c-415b-43ec-8f89-ff3ea7325cf3","timestamp":"2026-08-19T15:14:53.282Z"}
